.TH IMPRO 1 "" "impro" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
impro \- IDE with explorer, editor, live Markdown notes and terminal docks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B impro
[\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIpath\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the given paths in the impro window.
A folder becomes the project shown in the explorer and used by the terminal;
if several folders are given, the first one is used.
Files are opened in the editor.
When only files are given, the folder containing the first file is the project.
.PP
Without any path, impro opens the current directory.
When it is started without arguments from a launcher or from the home
directory, it reopens the last folder that was used instead.
.PP
A \fIfile://\fR URI is accepted wherever a path is.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage line and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
2 if a path does not exist, cannot be opened, or an option is not recognized.
